   "Northwind-negotiator": "competing",
   "Halcyon-researcher": "collaborating",
   "Halcyon-drafter": "competing",
   "Halcyon-negotiator": "compromising"
  },
  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": -2,
  "section_notes": "S1 requires strict 24-hour regulator reporting and 72-hour customer notice for fire, smoke, or hazardous overheating, including incidents whose cause is unconfirmed. S2 keeps the 55 °C test but has no automatic numerical failure-rate ceiling, while giving complete per-model results to customers and regulators without public publication. S3 sets new-unit shut-off at 24 months and retrofit at 6 years with a feasibility escape and interim instructions; S4 requires built-in suppression at 36 months; S5 mandates recall above 8/100k but defines recall as notification/remedy rather than automatic sales suspension, with 'promptly' notice."
 },
